      "text": "The Board also has overall responsibility for ensuring ongoing outsourcing decisions align with the outsourcing policy in a changing business environment [2].",
      "supported": true,
      "cited_supports": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Due diligence must assess the third party's resources, financial soundness, compatibility of systems, reputation, concentration, and (for foreign providers) the host-country environment [3].",
      "supported": true,
      "cited_supports": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The outsourcing policy must be principles-based and sufficiently detailed to guide staff, and Table 4 requires it to include \"links to other relevant policies\" (cross-referencing paragraph 4.8) and, under oversight, \"independent review and audit of compliance with legal and regulatory requirements and policies\" [4].",
      "supported": false,
      "cited_supports": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Firms may also rely on group-level policies and procedures, provided they comply with UK legal and regulatory obligations [6], and should share relevant internal policies (e.g. ICT, information security, operational resilience) with third-party providers [7].",
      "supported": true,
      "cited_supports": true
    },
    {
      "text": "SEBI prescribes a specific, standing obligation for auditor-led reviews of both the policy and the third party's capabilities, whereas the PRA embeds independent review and audit as one component within a broader, principles-based policy framework that explicitly cross-references other regulatory sources and permits reliance on group-level arrangements.",
